# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Happy Dog Runner — environment variables
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Copy to `.env` (or `.env.local`) and fill in per environment. Only variables
# prefixed with VITE_ are exposed to the client bundle (Vite convention).
# EVERY var below is OPTIONAL: the app runs correctly with all of them unset —
# analytics simply no-ops and sensible placeholder defaults are used.
# See src/config/env.ts for how each is read and its default.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# GA4 Measurement ID (e.g. G-XXXXXXXXXX). Leave blank to disable GA4.
VITE_GA4_ID=

# Meta (Facebook) Pixel ID (numeric). Leave blank to disable the Pixel.
VITE_FB_PIXEL_ID=

# Promo code shown on the results-screen CTA. Placeholder until client confirms.
VITE_PROMO_CODE=DOG10

# Base buy URL the CTA links to. UTM params are appended at runtime.
VITE_BUY_URL=https://tabletki.ua

# Campaign attribution (UTM) appended to the buy URL by buildBuyUrl().
VITE_UTM_SOURCE=happydogrunner
VITE_UTM_MEDIUM=game
VITE_UTM_CAMPAIGN=tick_protection

# Mirror every track() call to console.debug for QA. "true" to enable.
VITE_DEBUG_ANALYTICS=false
